    "https://ferrumcollege.applytojob.com/apply/Nwoj7NPyuQ/Grounds-Enhancement-Manager": {
      "title": "Grounds Enhancement Manager",
      "description": "Grounds Enhancement Manager - Ferrum College - Career Page Skip To Job Description View All Jobs View Our Website Thank you for visiting our Careers page. We invite you to explore our current openings and apply for positions that align with your qualifications and interests. Grounds Enhancement Manager Ferrum, VA Full Time Physical Plant Manager/Supervisor Share Grounds Enhancement Manager Department: Physical Plant Employment Type: Full-Time, 12-Months Salary: $45,000-$55,000 Workweek: 40 hours per week Employment Status: Exempt Who We Are? Ferrum College is committed to maintaining a safe, attractive, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, alumni, visitors, and the broader College community. The Grounds operation plays an important role in maintaining the appearance, functionality, safety, and sustainability of the Ferrum College campus. From daily landscape maintenance and athletic-field preparation to long-term improvements and environmental stewardship, our grounds team helps create an environment where the College community can learn, work, live, and thrive. What We're Looking For Ferrum College is seeking a motivated, experienced, and hands-on individual to lead the care, maintenance, and continued improvement of the College's campus grounds and athletic facilities. This position provides an opportunity for an experienced grounds and landscape professional to take a leading role in campus landscape operations, including daily maintenance, athletic-field preparation, landscape improvements, irrigation, staff leadership, budgeting, and sustainable practices. The successful candidate will combine strong horticultural and turf-management knowledge with practical leadership skills, attention to detail, and a commitment to maintaining a safe, attractive, and welcoming campus environment. Key Responsibilities Grounds & Landscape Operations Lead the daily maintenance and appearance of Ferrum College's campus grounds, including lawns, landscaped areas, trees, planting beds, sidewalks, and other exterior spaces. Develop and implement seasonal and long-term grounds maintenance plans. Establish priorities, work schedules, and maintenance standards for grounds operations. Monitor the condition of campus grounds and proactively address maintenance needs. Identify opportunities to improve the appearance, functionality, and sustainability of campus landscapes. Athletic Fields & Recreation Areas Oversee the maintenance and preparation of athletic fields and related outdoor facilities. Coordinate field preparation for practices, competitions, tournaments, and special events. Work closely with coaches, Athletics staff, and campus partners to understand and meet field requirements. Develop turf-management practices that promote safe, healthy, and high-quality playing surfaces. Respond to changing weather conditions and unexpected field-maintenance needs. Work occasional evenings, weekends, and overtime when necessary to support athletic and campus events. Team Leadership Supervise full-time and seasonal Grounds Technicians and student work-study employees. Recruit, train, schedule, coach, and evaluate employees. Establish clear expectations for productivity, workmanship, safety, and customer service. Create a positive, collaborative, and accountable team environment. Lead by example through hands-on involvement in grounds operations when needed. Planning, Budget & Resources Monitor expenditures and make informed purchasing and resource-allocation decisions. Evaluate equipment, materials, supplies, and contracted services for quality and cost effectiveness. Identify opportunities to reduce costs while maintaining or improving campus standards. Plan for equipment replacement, landscape improvements, and future operational needs. Landscape Enhancement & Projects Work with Physical Plant leadership, campus planners, architects, contractors, and other stakeholders on landscape projects and campus improvements. Help develop landscape plans that complement Ferrum College's campus character and long-term goals. Coordinate the implementation of planting, irrigation, turf, hardscape, and other exterior improvements. Evaluate existing landscapes and recommend improvements that provide long-term value. Sustainability & Environmental Stewardship Incorporate environmentally responsible practices into daily grounds operations. Promote efficient irrigation and water conservation. Utilize integrated pest management and responsible pesticide practices. Evaluate opportunities for native or climate-appropriate plantings, improved soil health, and reduced resource consumption. Encourage sustainable practices that improve campus appearance while reducing long-term maintenance costs. Safety & Compliance Maintain a safe work environment for employees, students, contractors, and campus visitors. Ensure grounds operations, equipment use, chemical applications, and athletic-field maintenance follow applicable safety requirements and industry standards. Maintain required records related to pesticide applications, equipment, safety, training, and compliance. Ensure staff receive appropriate safety training and use equipment and personal protective equipment properly. Who You Are? You are an experienced, hands-on grounds and landscape professional who takes pride in maintaining high standards and creating attractive, functional outdoor spaces. You understand the importance of effective grounds management and are comfortable balancing daily operations with long-term planning and improvement projects. You are a confident leader who can develop employees, establish expectations, manage resources, and work collaboratively with a variety of campus partners. You are knowledgeable about horticulture, turf management, irrigation, landscape maintenance, and grounds-maintenance equipment. You exercise good judgment, pay attention to detail, and take a proactive approach to identifying and addressing maintenance needs. You are also committed to safety, sustainability, water conservation, responsible pesticide practices, and environmentally responsible grounds management. Minimum Qualifications At least three to five years of progressively responsible experience in grounds maintenance, landscaping, horticulture, turf management, or a related field. Demonstrated experience leading or supervising grounds, landscape, turf, or maintenance personnel. Working knowledge of horticulture, landscape maintenance, irrigation systems, turf management, and grounds-maintenance equipment. Ability to organize multiple priorities and effectively manage day-to-day operations. Valid Virginia driver's license. Ability to work outdoors in varying weather conditions. Ability to perform physically demanding duties, including regularly lifting and carrying 20–50 pounds . Ability to work occasional evenings, weekends, overtime, and special events as operational needs require. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Horticulture, Landscape Architecture, Turf Management, Facilities Management, or a related field. Experience managing athletic fields or sports turf. Experience managing an operating budget or purchasing for a grounds or landscape operation. Virginia Pesticide Applicator Certification in Categories 3A and 3B, or willingness and ability to obtain certification. Experience working in a college, university, school, municipal, commercial, or other institutional environment. Knowledge of sustainable landscaping, water conservation, integrated pest management, and environmentally responsible grounds practices. What Makes This Opportunity Unique? The Grounds Enhancement Manager will have a visible and lasting impact on the Ferrum College experience. This is an opportunity to lead a dedicated grounds team while helping shape the appearance, functionality, and long-term sustainability of a distinctive college campus. We are looking for someone who takes pride in their work, enjoys developing people, understands quality grounds management, and sees opportunities to make a good landscape even better. If you are an experienced grounds or landscape professional ready to take the next step in your career and make a lasting impact on a college campus, we encourage you to apply. What We Offer At Ferrum College, you'll have the opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to the appearance and experience of our campus while leading a team dedicated to maintaining high standards. We offer: The opportunity to lead campus grounds and athletic-field operations. The opportunity to develop and implement landscape improvements. A collaborative campus environment. The opportunity to supervise, mentor, and develop grounds staff. Opportunities to incorporate sustainable and environmentally responsible practices. The opportunity to work closely with Athletics, Physical Plant leadership, campus planners, contractors, and other College partners. The opportunity to make a visible and lasting impact on the Ferrum College campus. Ready to Join Our Team? If you are an experienced grounds or landscape professional who is ready to take the next step in your career and make a lasting impact on a college campus, we encourage you to apply. Interested applicants should submit: Letter of Interest Resume Completed Employment Application Ferrum College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Address Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file The following questions are entirely optional. To comply with government Equal Employment Opportunity and/or Affirmative Action reporting regulations, we are requesting (but NOT requiring) that you enter this personal data. This information will not be used in connection with any employment decisions, and will be used solely as permitted by state and federal law. Your voluntary cooperation would be appreciated. Learn more . Gender Decline to answer Female Male Race/Ethnicity Decline to answer Hispanic or Latino White, not Hispanic or Latino Black or African-American, not Hispanic or Latino Asian, not Hispanic or Latino Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander, not Hispanic or Latino American Indian or Alaskan Native, not Hispanic or Latino Two or More Races, not Hispanic or Latino MENA (Middle Eastern and North African) Invitation for Job Applicants to Self-Identify as a U.S. Veteran A “disabled veteran” is one of the following: a veteran of the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service who is entitled to compensation (or who but for the receipt of military retired pay would be entitled to compensation) under laws administered by the Secretary of Veterans Affairs; or a person who was discharged or released from active duty because of a service-connected disability. A “recently separated veteran” means any veteran during the three-year period beginning on the date of such veteran's discharge or release from active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval, or air service. An “active duty wartime or campaign badge veteran” means a veteran who served on active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service during a war, or in a campaign or expedition for which a campaign badge has been authorized under the laws administered by the Department of Defense. An “Armed forces service medal veteran” means a veteran who, while serving on active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service, participated in a United States military operation for which an Armed Forces service medal was awarded pursuant to Executive Order 12985. Veteran status I IDENTIFY AS ONE OR MORE OF THE CLASSIFICATIONS OF PROTECTED VETERAN LISTED ABOVE I AM NOT A PROTECTED VETERAN I DON’T WISH TO ANSWER Voluntary Self-Identification of Disability Voluntary Self-Identification of Disability Form CC-305 OMB Control Number 1250-0005 Expires 07/31/2029 Why are you being asked to complete this form? We are a federal contractor or subcontractor. The law requires us to provide equal employment opportunity to qualified\n                                            people with disabilities. We have a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. The law says we\n                                            must measure our progress towards this goal. To do this, we must ask applicants and employees if they have a disability\n                                            or have ever had one. People can become disabled, so we need to ask this question at least every five years. Completing this form is voluntary, and we hope that you will choose to do so. Your answer is confidential. No one who\n                                            makes hiring decisions will see it. Your decision to complete the form and your answer will not harm you in any way. If you\n                                            want to learn more about the law or this form, visit the U.S. Department of Labor’s Office of Federal Contract Compliance\n                                            Programs (OFCCP) website at www.dol.gov/ofccp . How do you know if you have a disability? A disability is a condition that substantially limits one or more of your “major life activities.” If you have or have ever had\n                                            such a condition, you are a person with a disability. Disabilities include, but are not limited to: Alcohol or other substance use\n                                                disorder (not currently using\n                                                drugs illegally) Autoimmune disorder, for\n                                                example, lupus, fibromyalgia,\n                                                rheumatoid arthritis, HIV/AIDS Blind or low vision Cancer (past or present) Cardiovascular or heart\n                                                disease Celiac disease Cerebral palsy Deaf or serious difficulty\n                                                hearing Diabetes Disfigurement, for example,\n                                                disfigurement caused by burns,\n                                                wounds, accidents, or congenital\n                                                disorders Epilepsy or other seizure disorder Gastrointestinal disorders, for example,\n                                                Crohn's Disease, irritable bowel\n                                                syndrome Intellectual or developmental disability Mental health conditions, for example,\n                                                depression, bipolar disorder, anxiety\n                                                disorder, schizophrenia, PTSD Missing limbs or partially missing limbs Mobility impairment, benefiting from the\n                                                use of a wheelchair, scooter, walker,\n                                                leg brace(s) and/or other supports Nervous system condition, for example,\n                                                migraine headaches, Parkinson’s\n                                                disease, multiple sclerosis (MS) Neurodivergence, for example,\n                                                attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder\n                                                (ADHD), autism spectrum disorder,\n                                                dyslexia, dyspraxia, other learning\n                                                disabilities Partial or complete paralysis (any\n                                                cause) Pulmonary or respiratory conditions, for\n                                                example, tuberculosis, asthma,\n                                                emphysema Short stature (dwarfism) Traumatic brain injury Please check one of the boxes below: YES, I HAVE A DISABILITY, OR HAVE HAD ONE IN THE PAST NO, I DO NOT HAVE A DISABILITY AND HAVE NOT HAD ONE IN THE PAST I DO NOT WANT TO ANSWER PUBLIC BURDEN STATEMENT: According to the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 no persons are required to respond to a collection of information unless such collection displays a valid OMB control number. This survey should take about 5 minutes to complete. You must enter your name and date Name Date Human Check * Submit Application This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies. By selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers. Allow Reject All Powered by"
